        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karla Bonoff, Bonnie Raitt, Wynonna Judd, Lynn Anderson, Naomi Judd\n- Works: \"Home,\" \"Tell Me Why,\" \"Isn't It Always Love,\" Wild Heart of the Young\n- Groups: The Judds\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1980s, Wynonna Judd first rose to fame alongside her mother Naomi in the country music duo The Judds.\n- Wild Heart of the Young is the third album by singer-songwriter Karla Bonoff.\n- As a songwriter, Karla Bonoff wrote songs that were interpreted by other artists, including \"Home\" by Bonnie Raitt, \"Tell Me Why\" by Wynonna Judd, and \"Isn't It Always Love\" by Lynn Anderson.",
